overviewRequest:
Look at the {count, plural, one {# gap} other {# gaps}} Ontology Atlas found in this repository's agent harness and fill only the ones that need it. Before writing any file, show me its path and full text and wait for my yes.
Folder: {folder}
A gap means no harness file declares a path inside that domain. It does not mean nothing runs there: what reaches every domain still applies ({everywhere}).
{gaps}
For each gap, first decide whether this domain needs its own guide, block or check. If not, say why in one line and write nothing. If it does, propose the smallest file that names only that domain's paths: for Told, a .claude/rules/NAME.md with paths: or a FOLDER/AGENTS.md; for Gated, a PreToolUse hook script or a .githooks/ script that filters on those paths; for Watched, a package.json check that takes those paths or a workflow with paths:. A new hook script also needs its wiring entry under hooks in .claude/settings.json or in .codex/hooks.json; show that edit too, and do not change `permissions`. A Codex hook runs only after I trust it in /hooks, so tell me when you add one. A declared path fills the cell only when it contains one of the listed paths or sits inside one; paths-ignore does not count. Atlas reads only these forms: a package.json script named test, lint or typecheck, or test:NAME, lint:NAME or typecheck:NAME, whose command names a path of two or more segments such as src/features/x; an AGENTS.md directly inside a top-level folder; paths: as a YAML list with one path per line; and, in a hook script, the path as a quoted literal such as "src/features/x/". Ask before putting a copy under .codex/ or .agents/.
